# {{lb|en|transitive}} To find time or space for, amid other things.
#: {{ux|en|It'll be a tight schedule, but we can '''work''' you '''in'''.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[work out]] using a machine in between the sets of someone who is already using that machine.
#: {{ux|en|Is it okay if I '''work in''' while you rest?}}
# {{&lit|en|work|in}}
#: {{ux|en|Next, you have to '''work''' the eggs '''in''' the batter.}}
#: {{ux|en|He '''works in''' cybersecurity.}}

